---
import '../../styles/global.css';
import Navbar from '../../components/Navbar.astro';
---

<html lang="en">
    <head>
        <meta charset="UTF-8" />
        <title>Program – Q-LUMEN</title>
    </head>
    <body class="pt-16 md:pt-20">
        <Navbar />

        <!-- Hero Banner -->
        <section class="relative pt-32 pb-20 text-white text-center bg-cover bg-center bg-no-repeat" style="background-image: url('/images/Ulm2.jpg');">
            <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-black/50"></div>
            <div class="relative z-10">
                <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold mb-4">Program</h1>
                <p class="text-base md:text-lg max-w-2xl mx-auto px-6">Overview of the Q-LUMEN program</p>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Program Timeline -->
        <section class="max-w-7xl mx-auto py-16 px-6">
            <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-center mb-12 text-gray-800">Program Timeline</h2>

            <p class="text-center text-gray-600 mb-12 text-base max-w-4xl mx-auto">
                The following milestones outline the planned structure of the Q-LUMEN program from the international announcement to the final presentations.
            </p>

            <div class="space-y-10">
                <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-lg border border-gray-200 overflow-hidden">
                    <h3 class="bg-indigo-600 text-white text-xl font-semibold py-3 px-6 text-center">M1 · July 2026</h3>
                    <div class="p-6">
                        <p class="font-medium text-gray-900 mb-2">Program Announcement</p>
                        <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
                            In July 2026 at the latest, Q-LUMEN will be officially announced internationally, particularly across all participating
                            universities. The call for applications will be distributed through institutional channels and will target first-year Master’s
                            students in physics, quantum science, and related disciplines. This phase is intended to ensure broad visibility and attract a
                            diverse, highly qualified pool of applicants.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-lg border border-gray-200 overflow-hidden">
                    <h3 class="bg-indigo-600 text-white text-xl font-semibold py-3 px-6 text-center">M2 · September 2026</h3>
                    <div class="p-6">
                        <p class="font-medium text-gray-900 mb-2">Selection of Students</p>
                        <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
                            By September 2026, the selection process will be completed. Students will be chosen based on their academic background, motivation,
                            and interest in quantum information. Particular attention will be paid to creating a balanced cohort across institutions in order to
                            support diversity and effective international collaboration.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-lg border border-gray-200 overflow-hidden">
                    <h3 class="bg-indigo-600 text-white text-xl font-semibold py-3 px-6 text-center">M3 · October 2026</h3>
                    <div class="p-6">
                        <p class="font-medium text-gray-900 mb-2">In-Person Kickoff Meeting at Ulm University and Project Assignment</p>
                        <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
                            The programme will formally begin in October 2026 with an in-person kickoff meeting at Ulm University. During this event, students
                            and supervisors will meet, research topics will be introduced, and participants will be assigned to supervisors and international
                            project teams. This milestone is important for establishing personal connections and defining the scope and expectations of the
                            research projects.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-lg border border-gray-200 overflow-hidden">
                    <h3 class="bg-indigo-600 text-white text-xl font-semibold py-3 px-6 text-center">M4 · December 2026</h3>
                    <div class="p-6">
                        <p class="font-medium text-gray-900 mb-2">Research Visits to Partner Institutions</p>
                        <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
                            In December 2026, students will undertake short research visits to the participating groups, where feasible. These visits will
                            provide early exposure to the research environment, strengthen interaction with supervisors, and support the initial development of
                            the projects.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-lg border border-gray-200 overflow-hidden">
                    <h3 class="bg-indigo-600 text-white text-xl font-semibold py-3 px-6 text-center">M5 · April 2027</h3>
                    <div class="p-6">
                        <p class="font-medium text-gray-900 mb-2">Mid-Term Presentation (Online)</p>
                        <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
                            The mid-term phase will be marked by an online presentation event in April 2027. Student teams will present their progress, receive
                            structured feedback from supervisors and peers, and refine their research direction for the final phase of the programme.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-lg border border-gray-200 overflow-hidden">
                    <h3 class="bg-indigo-600 text-white text-xl font-semibold py-3 px-6 text-center">M6 · June 2027</h3>
                    <div class="p-6">
                        <p class="font-medium text-gray-900 mb-2">Final Meeting and Presentations</p>
                        <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
                            The programme will conclude in June 2027 with a final meeting, ideally held in person depending on available funding, and possibly
                            combined with the next kickoff meeting for the 2027 edition. Students will present their final results and reflect on their
                            experience within Q-LUMEN. This milestone represents the academic culmination of the programme and reinforces the international
                            collaboration established throughout the project.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Footer -->
        <footer class="bg-gray-900 text-white text-center py-6">
            <p class="mb-2">Q-LUMEN - the Quantum Leiden Ulm Milan ETH Network</p>

            <div class="flex items-center justify-center space-x-3">
                <p>Funded by – Global Teaching Lab UGO!</p>
                <img src="/images/Logo_UGo_white.png" alt="Global Teaching Lab UGO!" class="h-11 w-auto" />
            </div>
        </footer>
    </body>
</html>
